<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>brainboxemb</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/</link><description>Recent content on brainboxemb</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Parts and Suppliers</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/information/parts-and-suppliers/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/information/parts-and-suppliers/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Possible parts and suppliers for the HUB75 LED matrix display project, including the DIN rail, recessed handle, case latch and power cable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="din-rail"&gt;DIN rail&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.conrad.nl/nl/p/mean-well-ts35-7-5-1000-al-din-rail-aluminium-1000-mm-1-stuk-s-3557776.html"&gt;&lt;img src="https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/information/parts-and-suppliers/images/conrad-mean-well-ts35-7-5-1000-al.jpg" alt="Mean Well DIN rail"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Image/source: &lt;a href="https://www.conrad.nl/nl/p/mean-well-ts35-7-5-1000-al-din-rail-aluminium-1000-mm-1-stuk-s-3557776.html"&gt;Conrad&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.conrad.nl/nl/p/mean-well-ts35-7-5-1000-al-din-rail-aluminium-1000-mm-1-stuk-s-3557776.html"&gt;Conrad — Mean Well TS35/7.5-1000-AL DIN rail&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Aluminium DIN rail, 1000 mm long. Manufacturer part number: TS35/7.5-1000-AL.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="handle"&gt;Handle&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.fritz-events.nl/penn-elcom-h1025-inbouw-hoekgreep-zwart.html"&gt;&lt;img src="https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/information/parts-and-suppliers/images/fritz-events-penn-elcom-h1025-handle.jpg" alt="Penn Elcom H1025 recessed corner handle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Image/source: &lt;a href="https://www.fritz-events.nl/penn-elcom-h1025-inbouw-hoekgreep-zwart.html"&gt;Fritz-Events&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.fritz-events.nl/penn-elcom-h1025-inbouw-hoekgreep-zwart.html"&gt;Fritz-Events — Penn Elcom H1025 recessed corner handle&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.aweo.de/Penn-Elcom-H1025-Kanteneinbaugriff-schwarz"&gt;Additional picture at Aweo&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The listed dimensions are 150 × 57.2 × 57.2 mm.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>HUB75 Power Connections</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/electronics/power-connections/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/electronics/power-connections/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;A prototype concept for distributing 5 V power from one supply to the HUB75 LED matrix panels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="proposed-concept"&gt;Proposed concept&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/electronics/power-connections/images/power-distribution-concept.svg" alt="HUB75 power distribution prototype concept"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The prototype is deliberately simple:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1 × removable 20 A input&lt;/strong&gt; for the main 5 V supply;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2 × 4-pole barrier-strip terminals&lt;/strong&gt; for the HUB75 panel outputs;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1 × additional 2-pole 10 A screw terminal&lt;/strong&gt; for PCB / auxiliary 5 V;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;all mounted on a &lt;strong&gt;4 × 6 cm double-sided experiment PCB&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The two 4-pole barrier strips provide eight screw positions in total. Five positions are intended for the five HUB75 panel feeds, leaving three spare positions.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>TinyTronics Order List</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/information/order-lists/tinytronics/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/information/order-lists/tinytronics/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Current working order list for the HUB75 power-distribution prototype and controller service connection.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
	&lt;thead&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;th style="text-align: right"&gt;Qty&lt;/th&gt;
					&lt;th&gt;Part&lt;/th&gt;
					&lt;th&gt;Purpose&lt;/th&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
	&lt;/thead&gt;
	&lt;tbody&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.tinytronics.nl/en/tools-and-mounting/prototyping-supplies/experiment-pcbs/experiment-pcb-4cm*6cm-double-sided"&gt;Experiment PCB 4 × 6 cm, double-sided&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Mechanical carrier for the first power-distribution prototype&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;2&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.tinytronics.nl/en/cables-and-connectors/connectors/screw-terminals/barrier-strip-screw-terminal-4p-7.62mm"&gt;Barrier Strip Screw Terminal, 4p, 7.62 mm&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Two 4-pole HUB75 power-distribution rails&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.tinytronics.nl/en/cables-and-connectors/connectors/screw-terminals/terminal-block-for-removable-screw-terminal-90-2p-5.08mm"&gt;Terminal Block for Removable Screw Terminal, 90°, 2p, 5.08 mm&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;PCB-side connector for the removable 20 A main 5 V input&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.tinytronics.nl/en/cables-and-connectors/connectors/screw-terminals/removable-screw-terminal-2p-5.08mm"&gt;Removable Screw Terminal, 2p, 5.08 mm&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Cable-side plug for the removable 20 A main 5 V input&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.tinytronics.nl/en/cables-and-connectors/connectors/screw-terminals/2-pin-screw-terminal-block-connector-5.08mm-distance"&gt;2 Pin Screw Terminal Block Connector, 5.08 mm&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Additional 10 A PCB / auxiliary 5 V connection&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;—&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.tinytronics.nl/en/cables-and-connectors/connectors/screw-terminals/2-pin-screw-terminal-block-connector-2.54mm-distance"&gt;2 Pin Screw Terminal Block Connector, 2.54 mm&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Compact alternative for a lower-current auxiliary connection; rated 6 A max and 1 mm² wire max. Not included in the current order because it is not in stock.&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.tinytronics.nl/en/cables-and-connectors/cables-and-adapters/usb/usb-b/micro-usb-usb-b-extention-cable-with-mount-50cm"&gt;Micro USB – USB-B Extension Cable with Mount, 50 cm&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Bring the internal controller USB connection to an externally accessible panel-mount USB-B socket&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.tinytronics.nl/nl/schakelaars/manuele-schakelaars/drukknoppen-en-schakelaars/zwarte-drukknop-16mm-reset?sort=p.price&amp;amp;order=ASC"&gt;Black Push Button 16 mm - Reset&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Candidate momentary service/reset button for the enclosure&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
	&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The power-distribution items above correspond to the &lt;a href="../../../concepts-and-ideas/electronics/power-connections/"&gt;current power-distribution prototype concept&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Woodworking Videos</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/woodworking/videos/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/woodworking/videos/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Useful woodworking videos for building and finishing the HUB75 display enclosure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The videos below are kept as practical references. The thumbnail is stored locally with this page; clicking the image or title opens the original YouTube video.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="finishing-plywood-edges-with-solid-oak"&gt;Finishing plywood edges with solid oak&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class="reference-example"&gt;
 &lt;figure class="reference-example__figure"&gt;
 &lt;a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qbDb97wQ-r0" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;
 &lt;img class="reference-example__image"
 src="https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/woodworking/videos/images/youtube-oak-plywood-edges-w320.webp"
 alt="YouTube thumbnail for a video about finishing exposed plywood edges with solid oak"
 loading="lazy"&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
 &lt;figcaption class="reference-example__figcaption"&gt;
 &lt;span class="reference-example__caption"&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qbDb97wQ-r0" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;YouTube — Using oak on the exposed edges of plywood&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;span class="reference-example__note"&gt;Shows how a strip of solid oak can be applied to an exposed plywood edge for a cleaner and more durable finish.&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;span class="reference-example__source"&gt;Source: &lt;a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qbDb97wQ-r0" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;YouTube&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;/figcaption&gt;
 &lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This may be useful for the enclosure because plywood edges remain visible after cutting.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Wooden Enclosure Design Considerations</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/enclosure/wooden-enclosure/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/enclosure/wooden-enclosure/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Two enclosure concepts are currently being considered for the HUB75 LED matrix display.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="rear-assembly"&gt;Rear assembly&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this concept, the enclosure is assembled from the rear.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The display panels, electronics and other internal parts are mounted from the back of the enclosure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/enclosure/wooden-enclosure/images/system_a_assembled.png" alt="Rear assembly concept, assembled"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/enclosure/wooden-enclosure/images/system_a_exploded.png" alt="Rear assembly concept, exploded"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="removable-top-cover"&gt;Removable top cover&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this concept, the top panel of the enclosure acts as a removable lid.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The plexiglass front and possibly a separate frame containing the LED panels can be inserted into the enclosure from the top.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Aluminium Frame Design Considerations</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/enclosure/aluminium-frame/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/enclosure/aluminium-frame/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;The internal frame uses 20 × 20 mm aluminium construction profiles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="main-dimensions"&gt;Main dimensions&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
	&lt;thead&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;th&gt;Dimension&lt;/th&gt;
					&lt;th style="text-align: right"&gt;Value&lt;/th&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
	&lt;/thead&gt;
	&lt;tbody&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Overall width&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;840 mm&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Overall height&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;360 mm&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Horizontal profiles&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;840 mm&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Vertical profiles&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;320 mm&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Profile size&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td style="text-align: right"&gt;20 × 20 mm&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
	&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The overall height consists of a 20 mm top profile, a 320 mm vertical profile and a 20 mm bottom profile.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="panel-mounting"&gt;Panel mounting&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The five HUB75 panels will be mounted to the frame using custom brackets.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Power Distribution Examples</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/electronics/power-distribution-examples/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/electronics/power-distribution-examples/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Examples that inspired the HUB75 power-distribution concept.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These are &lt;strong&gt;references, not the proposed design&lt;/strong&gt;. Where a verified reference image is available, it is shown as a small thumbnail (maximum 300 px wide). Clicking an image or product name opens the original product page, and the image source is written out explicitly below the thumbnail.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="screw-terminal-distribution"&gt;Screw-terminal distribution&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class="reference-example"&gt;
 &lt;figure class="reference-example__figure"&gt;
 &lt;a href="https://www.amazon.nl/Evemodel-Distribution-Ingangen-Uitgangen-Voltage/dp/B08149N2Y2" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;
 &lt;img class="reference-example__image"
 src="https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/electronics/power-distribution-examples/images/rjs-trains-evemodel-pcb005-w320.webp"
 alt="Evemodel PCB005 power distribution board with two rows of screw terminals"
 loading="lazy"&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
 &lt;figcaption class="reference-example__figcaption"&gt;
 &lt;span class="reference-example__caption"&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.amazon.nl/Evemodel-Distribution-Ingangen-Uitgangen-Voltage/dp/B08149N2Y2" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Evemodel PCB005 power distribution board&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;span class="reference-example__note"&gt;Useful reference for a central input feeding two long rows of screw-terminal outputs.&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;span class="reference-example__source"&gt;Source: &lt;a href="https://rjstrains.com/products/evemodel-pcb005-1x-power-distribution-board-3-inputs-2-x-10-outputs-for-dc-ac-voltage" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;RJ&amp;#39;s Trains&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;/figcaption&gt;
 &lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class="reference-example"&gt;
 &lt;figure class="reference-example__figure"&gt;
 &lt;a href="https://www.amazon.nl/dp/B093PWRJS9" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;
 &lt;img class="reference-example__image"
 src="https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/electronics/power-distribution-examples/images/amazon-wayintop-power-distribution-w320.webp"
 alt="WayinTop double-layer power distribution boards"
 loading="lazy"&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
 &lt;figcaption class="reference-example__figcaption"&gt;
 &lt;span class="reference-example__caption"&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.amazon.nl/dp/B093PWRJS9" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;WayinTop double-layer power distribution board&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;span class="reference-example__note"&gt;Reference for separate positive and negative rails with many repeated screw-terminal positions.&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;span class="reference-example__source"&gt;Source: &lt;a href="https://www.amazon.nl/dp/B093PWRJS9" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Amazon&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;/figcaption&gt;
 &lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2 id="plug-in-distribution"&gt;Plug-in distribution&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class="reference-example"&gt;
 &lt;figure class="reference-example__figure"&gt;
 &lt;a href="https://buildingblockrobotics.com/products/xt30-power-distribution-board" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;
 &lt;img class="reference-example__image"
 src="https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/electronics/power-distribution-examples/images/building-block-robotics-xt30-power-distribution-w320.webp"
 alt="Building Block Robotics XT30 power distribution board"
 loading="lazy"&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
 &lt;figcaption class="reference-example__figcaption"&gt;
 &lt;span class="reference-example__caption"&gt;&lt;a href="https://buildingblockrobotics.com/products/xt30-power-distribution-board" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Building Block Robotics XT30 Power Distribution Board&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;span class="reference-example__note"&gt;One input feeding three compact, individually disconnectable XT30 outputs.&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;span class="reference-example__source"&gt;Source: &lt;a href="https://buildingblockrobotics.com/products/xt30-power-distribution-board" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Building Block Robotics&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;/figcaption&gt;
 &lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class="reference-example"&gt;
 &lt;figure class="reference-example__figure"&gt;
 &lt;a href="https://eckstein-shop.de/xt30-6-port-parallel-power-distribution-board-pla-case" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;
 &lt;img class="reference-example__image"
 src="https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/electronics/power-distribution-examples/images/eckstein-robotics-xt30-6-port-power-distribution-w320.webp"
 alt="Eckstein ER-OA001 XT30 6-port parallel power distribution board in a PLA enclosure"
 loading="lazy"&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
 &lt;figcaption class="reference-example__figcaption"&gt;
 &lt;span class="reference-example__caption"&gt;&lt;a href="https://eckstein-shop.de/xt30-6-port-parallel-power-distribution-board-pla-case" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Eckstein Robotics XT30 6-port parallel power distribution board&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;span class="reference-example__note"&gt;One XT30 input feeding six parallel XT30 outputs in a compact PLA protective enclosure.&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;span class="reference-example__source"&gt;Source: &lt;a href="https://eckstein-shop.de/xt30-6-port-parallel-power-distribution-board-pla-case" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Eckstein Robotics&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;/figcaption&gt;
 &lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2 id="what-is-useful-for-our-concept"&gt;What is useful for our concept&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The screw-terminal examples are closest to the current prototype idea: a central supply feeding repeated connection points.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Finishing the Wooden Enclosure</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/enclosure/finishing/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/enclosure/finishing/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;The current preference is a simple silver-grey wood stain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The existing display enclosures appear to have a black finish. A lighter colour is preferred for the new display because it may be used in direct sunlight.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A silver-grey finish should:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;be easy to apply;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;require no more than two coats;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;be suitable for the inside and outside of the enclosure;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;provide a lighter finish than black;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;allow some wood grain to remain visible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id="edge-sealing"&gt;Edge sealing&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The sawn edges of the plywood should be sealed before applying the final finish.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Okoumé Wood Suppliers</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/information/wood-suppliers/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/information/wood-suppliers/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This page contains suppliers of Okoumé plywood for the HUB75 LED matrix display project.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prices were checked in July 2026 and may change over time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This first overview focuses mainly on quarter-size sheets of approximately 61 × 125 cm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A separate overview of full-size sheets may be added later, including suppliers that can cut the material to size.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;h2 id="surface-types"&gt;Surface types&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id="unprimed"&gt;Unprimed&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Natural wood surface without primer or foil.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="primed"&gt;Primed&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Factory-applied primer intended as a base for paint.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Feet for the Enclosure</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/enclosure/feet/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/enclosure/feet/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This page contains possible feet for the HUB75 display enclosure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prices were checked in July 2026 and may change over time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;h2 id="requirements"&gt;Requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The feet should:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;protect the enclosure and the surface underneath it;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;provide some grip;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;keep the enclosure stable;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;be suitable for mounting underneath the wooden enclosure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id="hornbach"&gt;Hornbach&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id="tarrox-door-stopper"&gt;TARROX door stopper&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.hornbach.nl/p/tarrox-deurstopper-o-20x10-mm-kunststof-zwart-4-stuks/10565300/"&gt;Hornbach — TARROX door stopper Ø 20 × 10 mm, black, 4 pieces&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;table&gt;
	&lt;thead&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;th&gt;Property&lt;/th&gt;
					&lt;th&gt;Value&lt;/th&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
	&lt;/thead&gt;
	&lt;tbody&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Diameter&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;20 mm&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Height&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;10 mm&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Material&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Plastic&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Colour&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Black&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Quantity&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;4&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
			&lt;tr&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;Price&lt;/td&gt;
					&lt;td&gt;€1.60 including VAT&lt;/td&gt;
			&lt;/tr&gt;
	&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These are small and inexpensive. The product is sold as a door stopper rather than as a dedicated equipment foot.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Reference Files</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/information/reference-files/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/information/reference-files/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Files preserved from the original HUB75 project knowledge pages.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="hub75-module-datasheet"&gt;HUB75 module datasheet&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/information/reference-files/2277_P5_320x160mm_64x32&amp;#43;pixel.pdf"&gt;Adafruit P5 320 × 160 mm, 64 × 32 pixel panel datasheet&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="cost-estimate"&gt;Cost estimate&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/information/reference-files/20260718_HUB_display_cost_estimate.pdf"&gt;Aluminium extrusion cost estimate — 2026-07-18&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="openscad-source"&gt;OpenSCAD source&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/information/reference-files/system-examples.scad"&gt;Download system-examples.scad&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The OpenSCAD file contains the two enclosure concepts shown on the wooden-enclosure design page.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Aluminium Extrusion Frame Idea</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/enclosure/aluminium-extrusion-frame/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/enclosure/aluminium-extrusion-frame/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Aluminium extrusion could be used to create a rigid and modular frame around the LED panels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.instructables.com/Simple-Extruded-Aluminum-Frame-for-LED-Panels/"&gt;Simple Extruded Aluminum Frame for LED Panels&lt;/a&gt; — practical example of constructing an LED-panel frame using aluminium extrusion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://hackaday.com/2021/02/23/useful-build-tips-for-making-led-panel-frames/"&gt;Useful Build Tips for Making LED Panel Frames&lt;/a&gt; — notes about measurements, magnetic mounting, wiring, DIN rail, controller mounting and power supplies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.instructables.com/Simple-Extruded-Aluminum-Frame-for-LED-Panels/"&gt;&lt;img src="https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/enclosure/aluminium-extrusion-frame/images/instructables-simple-extruded-aluminum-frame-led-panels.webp" alt="Simple extruded aluminium frame for LED panels"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Image/source: &lt;a href="https://www.instructables.com/Simple-Extruded-Aluminum-Frame-for-LED-Panels/"&gt;Instructables&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Hinge Ideas</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/enclosure/hinges/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/enclosure/hinges/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This page collects &lt;strong&gt;3D-printable hinge ideas and real-world mechanism references&lt;/strong&gt; for the HUB75 display enclosure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The examples are starting points rather than final selections. The main questions are how far the panel must open, whether the hinge should remain hidden when closed, and how much clearance the mechanism needs around the enclosure edge.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="stop-and-180-degree-hinges"&gt;Stop and 180-degree hinges&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id="stop-hinge"&gt;Stop hinge&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div class="reference-example"&gt;
 &lt;figure class="reference-example__figure"&gt;
 &lt;a href="https://makerworld.com/nl/models/2644412-stop-hinge#profileId-2922394" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;
 &lt;img class="reference-example__image"
 src="https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/001-hub75-display/concepts-and-ideas/enclosure/hinges/images/makerworld-stop-hinge-w320.webp"
 alt="3D-printed stop hinge"
 loading="lazy"&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
 &lt;figcaption class="reference-example__figcaption"&gt;
 &lt;span class="reference-example__caption"&gt;&lt;a href="https://makerworld.com/nl/models/2644412-stop-hinge#profileId-2922394" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;MakerWorld — Stop Hinge&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;span class="reference-example__note"&gt;A printable hinge with an integrated stop that limits its maximum opening angle.&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;span class="reference-example__source"&gt;Source: &lt;a href="https://makerworld.com/nl/models/2644412-stop-hinge#profileId-2922394" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;MakerWorld&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;/figcaption&gt;
 &lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This may be useful for a lid or support panel that must stop at a defined angle without a separate cable or support arm.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Cal Bryant — pushing OpenSCAD further</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/knowledge/software/cad/openscad/log/2026/2026-10-30-cal-bryant-openscad-projects/</link><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/knowledge/software/cad/openscad/log/2026/2026-10-30-cal-bryant-openscad-projects/</guid><description>Three Cal Bryant articles showing OpenSCAD used for large prints, fully parametric speaker cabinets and disciplined larger-project workflows.</description></item><item><title>Double Your Storage</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/daily/diy-fab/2026/10/2026-10-30-double-your-storage/</link><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/daily/diy-fab/2026/10/2026-10-30-double-your-storage/</guid><description>A workshop-storage video showing a compact vertical/mobile tool-storage approach; saved as a useful DIY fabrication reference.</description></item><item><title>FNIRSI DLA-16/32 Plus Logic Analyzer</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/daily/software-embedded/2026/10/2026-10-30-fnirsi-dla-16-32-plus-logic-analyzer/</link><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/daily/software-embedded/2026/10/2026-10-30-fnirsi-dla-16-32-plus-logic-analyzer/</guid><description>A relatively low-cost 16/32-channel USB 3.0 logic analyzer with up to 1 GSa/s sampling, 4 Gbit memory and 120+ protocol decoders.</description></item><item><title>ModelRift OpenSCAD models</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/knowledge/software/cad/openscad/log/2026/2026-10-30-modelrift-openscad-models/</link><pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/knowledge/software/cad/openscad/log/2026/2026-10-30-modelrift-openscad-models/</guid><description>ModelRift combines OpenSCAD source, interactive parameter controls and AI-assisted model generation in a browser-based model gallery.</description></item><item><title>Is This The Only Instrument You Need?</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/daily/hackaday/2026/10/2026-10-29-is-this-the-only-instrument-you-need/</link><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/daily/hackaday/2026/10/2026-10-29-is-this-the-only-instrument-you-need/</guid><description>Pico.Lab combines several bench instruments around an RP2350; especially interesting is its browser-based windowed GUI served directly over USB networking.</description></item><item><title>Lightweight Linux distribution alternatives</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/005-brainbox-zero/log/20261029-lightweight-linux-distribution-alternatives/</link><pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/005-brainbox-zero/log/20261029-lightweight-linux-distribution-alternatives/</guid><description>Reference for possible smaller Linux distributions for Brainbox Zero.</description></item><item><title>Button SHIM reference and mounting</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/005-brainbox-zero/log/20261027-button-shim-reference-and-mounting/</link><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/projects/2026/005-brainbox-zero/log/20261027-button-shim-reference-and-mounting/</guid><description>Button SHIM availability, pin use and a mounting idea for Brainbox Zero.</description></item><item><title>Gardening With…OpenSCAD?</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/knowledge/software/cad/openscad/log/2026/2026-10-01-gardening-with-openscad/</link><pubDate>Thu, 01 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/knowledge/software/cad/openscad/log/2026/2026-10-01-gardening-with-openscad/</guid><description>Hackaday example of using OpenSCAD to plan a complete vertical-garden assembly rather than only producing parts for manufacturing.</description></item><item><title>Unofficial MakerWorld PMM OpenSCAD Reference</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/knowledge/software/cad/openscad/log/2026/2026-05-04-makerworld-pmm-openscad-reference/</link><pubDate>Mon, 04 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/knowledge/software/cad/openscad/log/2026/2026-05-04-makerworld-pmm-openscad-reference/</guid><description>Mindflakes article and companion repository collecting MakerWorld Parametric Model Maker rules and OpenSCAD-specific reference material.</description></item><item><title>AI-assisted content</title><link>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/ai-assisted-content/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://brainboxemb.github.io/notes/ai-assisted-content/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Parts of this site are created, edited or researched with AI assistance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI is used as a practical tool for drafting, restructuring notes, summarising supplied references, researching technical details and maintaining the site. The resulting content is reviewed during normal use of the site, but it may still contain errors, outdated information, incomplete interpretations or incorrect conclusions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For technical details that matter for safety, compatibility, purchasing decisions or implementation, verify the information against the original manufacturer, project, standards documentation or other primary source.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>